<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen up in early 1997.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen up in early 1997.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are expected to rise in early 1997 due to the wedding season, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Demand for jewellery would rise in January and February due to the wedding season, which pushes gold rates up in the local markets, one dealer said.</p>
<p>Silver rates had remained unchanged as there was no demand for it for jewellery, he said.</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grammes SUNDAY   Dec 22</p>
<p>							 5,263    5,130</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,286    7,286</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
